.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt LID-POLICY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lid-policy
.Nd set the ACPI lid-switch policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm awake
.Nm Cm s0ix
.Nm Cm s3
.Nm Cm toggle
.Nm Cm status
.Nm Cm suspend-s0ix
.Nm Cm suspend-s3
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends one command to
.Xr lid-switchd 8
and reads one line back.
.Cm awake
sets
.Va hw.acpi.lid_switch_state
to
.Cm NONE
and shows the awake glyph.
.Cm s0ix
sets it to suspend-to-idle
.Pq Cm suspend_to_idle or Cm s2idle ,
shows the sleep glyph, and makes that the type
.Cm toggle
writes.
.Cm s3
sets it to firmware suspend
.Pq Cm fw_suspend or Cm s2mem ,
shows the same sleep glyph, and makes that the type
.Cm toggle
writes.
.Cm toggle
flips between
.Cm NONE
and that sleep type and shows the glyph for the new state.
.Cm awake
shows the awake glyph and does not change which sleep type
.Cm toggle
writes.
.Cm status
prints the current value and does not show a glyph.
Suspend-to-idle is reported as
.Cm suspend_to_idle
or
.Cm s2idle .
Firmware suspend is reported as
.Cm fw_suspend
or
.Cm s2mem .
Which word is printed depends on the kernel.
A script that reads this output should accept both names of a type so that
it does not need the kernel version or
.Va kern.power.supported_stype .
.Pp
.Cm suspend-s0ix
and
.Cm suspend-s3
ask the daemon to suspend now.
They do not show a glyph.
.Pp
The glyph is
.Xr bosd 1
.Cm lid-awake
or
.Cm lid-s0ix .
When
.Nm bosd
is not in
.Ev PATH ,
the policy still changes.
.Pp
The socket is
.Ev lid_switchd_socket ,
or
.Pa /var/run/lid-switchd.sock
when that is unset.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "lid_switchd_socket"
.It Ev lid_switchd_socket
Control socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/lid-switchd.sock .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the daemon accepts the command.
It exits 1 when the socket is missing or the reply is an error.
A missing or unknown argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr lid-wake-toggle 1 ,
.Xr lid-switchd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
